riables for the TDMA scheme. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n real(kind=WP), intent(in) :: coeff (NL,NS,NBCS:NBCE,NACC) real(kind=WP), intent(out) :: a (n,NBCS:NBCE,NBCS:NBCE,NACC) real(kind=WP), intent(out) :: b (n,NBCS:NBCE,NBCS:NBCE,NACC) real(kind=WP), intent(out) :: c (n,NBCS:NBCE,NBCS:NBCE,NACC) real(kind=WP), intent(out) :: d (n,NBCS:NBCE,NBCS:NBCE,NACC) public  subroutine Prepare_LHS_coeffs_for_operations () Preparing coefficients for TDMA calculation.\nScope:  mpi    called-freq    xdomain\n        all    once           all Arguments None private  subroutine buildup_ghost_cells_C (fi, ibc, fc, opt_fbc, opt_dp) dp(n) is the round-trip distance used to apply a Neumann gradient, i.e.\ntwice the distance from the boundary to the interior node being mirrored:\ndp(1) = ( yc(1) - yp(1) ) * 2                  ! mirrors fi(1),    -> h  uniform\ndp(3) = ( yc(2) - yp(1) ) * 2                  ! mirrors fi(2),    -> 3h uniform\ndp(2) = ( yp(np) - yc(nc  ) ) * 2              ! mirrors fi(nc)\ndp(4) = ( yp(np) - yc(nc-1) ) * 2              ! mirrors fi(nc-1)\nNote dp(3) /= 2*dp(1) for cell-centred input: the second cell centre sits at\n3h/2, not 2h. That shortcut only holds for the p-node variant below.\n                  BC                                BC\n     _| . | . || . | . | ...___| . | . || . | . | .__\n        -1     0      1     2            nc-1   nc    nc+1   nc+2 Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=WP), intent(in) :: fi (:) integer, intent(in) :: ibc (2) real(kind=WP), intent(inout) :: fc (-1:2) real(kind=WP), intent(in), optional :: opt_fbc (4) real(kind=WP), intent(in), optional :: opt_dp (4) private  subroutine buildup_ghost_cells_P (fi, ibc, fp, opt_fbc, opt_dp) dp(1) = ( yp(2) - yp(1) ) * 2\ndp(3) = ( yp(3) - yp(1) ) * 2\ndp(2) = ( yp(np) - yp(np-1) ) * 2\ndp(4) = ( yp(np) - yp(np-2) ) * 2\n                  BC                                BC\n     _| . | . || . | . | 